        "answer": "The new connection is a phase-aware input map, not another reconstruction of the old damage predicate. Ordinary spawn writes sessionteam=self.team and sessionstate=playing and refreshes spawntime before later on_player_spawned/insertion work. A redeploy batch merely threads the spawnclient route, whose admission/queue branches mean selection is not proof of a fresh spawn clock. Spectator camera/sessionstate and spectator sessionteam are distinct; should_do_player_damage vetoes only the latter. No explicit candocombat writer is present in the 2,632 frozen GSC/CSC references; its effective producer and original value remain unknown. Insertion holds, begin/teleport flags and HMH doublejump/fallheight branches do not directly write those inputs in the cited spans. Spawn protection is the script elapsed<=cached-ms comparison, checked here only with bit 8; equality counts. Native invulnerabili [excerpt; exact source record identified separately]",
